id: lesson.consolidation
category: lesson
status: verified
date: 2026-08-24
content: Frequent patterns should be consolidated into permanent procedural memories
  (skills). One-time fixes are temporary; encoded patterns are permanent.
notes: 'Pattern frequency → procedural memory (skill)

  One-time fixes → working memory (temporary)

  Skills are reusable across sessions and cycles

  The ReflectionEngine should identify patterns worth consolidating

  SynthesisEngine should recommend skill creation for recurring patterns

  '
metadata: {}
prerequisites: []
blocking: []
tags:
- consolidation
- skills
- procedural-memory
- patterns
- permanence
---
id: lesson.quality_tracking
category: lesson
status: verified
date: 2026-08-24
content: Quality must be measured, not assumed. Track test pass rates, artifact counts,
  and execution duration trends across cycles.
notes: 'Metrics: test pass rate, number of artifacts created, execution time

  Trends matter more than single-cycle results

  Quality improvement is the goal of every self-improvement cycle

  If metrics are declining, the system should reflect and adjust

  Synthesis guidance should include quality recommendations

  '
metadata: {}
prerequisites: []
blocking: []
tags:
- quality
- metrics
- tracking
- improvement
- trends
